    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e7ab7f4b-d656-510e-82d2-d23a78f12dcb" activityNameId="9a65159d-4319-5340-ab8e-be22454b4019" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Lithium fluoride, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Lithium fluoride, at plant
The dataset can be used for example as base material to produce  LiPF6. Data are based on patents. ;
CAS number: 007789-24-4; 
Formula: LiMN2O4; 
Synonyms: LiF; 
UUID: 2d2359ec-2448-3873-9a03-d623df33ac95
This dataset includes the reaction of lithium carbonate  with hydrogen fluoride in an autoklave to lithium fluoride, carbon dioxide and water. The reaction temperatur is 21°C (no need to cool or heat). Energy consumption to evaporate water to dry the salt and CO2 emissions to air from the reaction are calculated. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.
Location: Some Swiss or  European datasets are used for global processes.
Technology: This dataset includes a method of producing lithium fluoride out of lithium carbonate and hydrogen fluoride under ambient conditions (no heating, no cooling, no pressure). Lithium carbonate conversion is 95.5%. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: patent, website, ecoinvent 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2d2359ec-2448-3873-9a03-d623df33ac95.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
